    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://www.blind-magazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/dscn3141copyjpg-vi.jpg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "Blind Magazine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Konstantin Petrov’s photographs remain one of the only interior records of the World Trade Center from its final months, empty rooms and quiet views taken by someone with no reason to think they would matter. Twenty-five years later, they stand on their own: a night-shift electrician’s private archive, published now as the last look inside a building that no longer exists."
    }
  ]
